ception:\n95\t       sys.exit(0)\n96\t   lines = []\n97\t   for frame in frames[:30]:\n98\t       lineno = frame.get(\"lineno\")\n99\t       if not isinstance(lineno, int):\n100\t           continue\n101\t       path = frame.get(\"abs_path\") or frame.get(\"filename\") or \"\"\n102\t       func = frame.get(\"function\") or \"unknown\"\n103\t       lines.append(\"%s:%s in %s\" % (os.path.basename(path), lineno, func))\n104\t   if lines:\n105\t       print(\"stack_trace=%d frames\" % len(lines))\n106\t       print(\"\\n\".join(lines))\n107\t   ' \"${event_body}\")\"\n108\t   frames_rc=$?\n109\t   set -e\n110\t   if [ \"${frames_rc}\" -ne 0 ] || [ -z \"${frames}\" ]; then\n111\t     printf 'stack_trace unavailable (no exception entry)\\n'\n112\t   else\n113\t     printf '%s\\n' \"${frames}\"\n114\t   fi\n115\t   ```\n116\t   - The frame line format is exactly `<file>:<line> in <function>` where `<file>` is the basename of `abs_path` (falling back to `filename`), `<line>` is `lineno`, and `<function>` is the frame's `function` (empty → `unknown`).\n117\t   - The 30-frame cap is the first 30 frames from `stacktrace.frames` AFTER skipping frames without a numeric `lineno`; the header `stack_trace=<N> frames` reports N = the number of emitted frame lines (N ≤ 30).\n118\t   - If the python command exits non-zero OR produces empty output — malformed/truncated JSON, a missing exception entry, or all frames skipped — emit `stack_trace unavailable (no exception entry)` and continue (exit 0). This maps the Failure Modes rows \"malformed/truncated\" and \"missing exception entry\" to this marker.\n119\t\n120\t5. **Update the header comment (DB5).** Update the block of `#` comments at the top of `scripts/sentry-read.sh` to document:\n121\t   - the new `stack_trace=<N> frames` header line followed by `file:line in function` frame lines;\n122\t   - the best-effort `stack_trace unavailable (<reason>)` marker (event fetch failure never fails the run);\n123\t   - the fixed 30-frame cap