{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_fb5801b5a91c43f491077436","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-adcc1bfc91abff4e","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/scripts/sentry-create-tasks.sh"}}],"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8adc49446a5650c3","session_id":"5d6cc7de-1074-471b-be5a-1eef1a32f0f2","uuid":"6125bcb6-d6c1-4782-8125-751ab08c7349","timestamp":"2026-08-31T22:35:04.642Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-auditor","task_description":"Audit prompt 1"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac052d05462de8f0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tspec: [\"001-sentry-read-event-payload\"]\n3\tstatus: draft\n4\tcreated: \"2026-09-01T12:00:00Z\"\n5\t---\n6\t\n7\t# Add a deterministic mock-API test for the Sentry read script\n8\t\n9\t<summary>\n10\t- Adds a self-contained bash test that drives the read script against a local fixture HTTP server\n11\t- The fixture server is a python3 http.server bound only to 127.0.0.1 on an ephemeral port, so no external network, Docker socket, or real credentials are involved — it is container-executable\n12\t- The test asserts the full AC1–AC5 output contract: the 7 metadata keys in their frozen order, the `file:line in function` frame format, the fixed 30-frame cap, and the no-raw-payload / no-PII invariant\n13\t- Bare numeric id and full-URL invocations are shown to produce byte-identical output\n14\t- Failure stubs (no events, no exception entry, auth denied) each produce exactly one `stack_trace unavailable` marker while the metadata block stays intact\n15\t- The harness exits non-zero with a named FAIL message on any assertion miss, so it is safe to run in CI\n16\t</summary>\n17\t\n18\t<objective>\n19\tCreate a deterministic, container-executable test harness that locks the Sentry read script's output contract (acceptance criteria AC1–AC5) without any live Sentry access, so the frame cap and the no-PII invariant are verifiable now and guard against regressions later.\n20\t</objective>\n21\t\n22\t<context>\n23\tRead CLAUDE.md for project conventions. There is no project-level CLAUDE.md at the repo root.\n24\t\n25\tRead these files before making changes:\n26\t\n27\t- `scripts/sentry-read.sh` — the script under test. This prompt depends on the preceding prompt having extended it to emit `stack_trace=<N> frames` / `file:line in function` lines and `stack_trace unavailable (<reason>)` markers. If the script does NOT yet contain an `events/latest` fetch, STOP and report that this prompt is out of order.\n28\t- `scripts/sentry-create-tasks.sh` — the repo's established style for `mktemp` + `trap 'rm -f ...' EXIT` cleanup and `python3 -c '...'` JSON handling; mirror it.\n29\t\n30\tThe assertion contract is defined in `specs/in-progress/001-sentry-read-event-payload.md` — Acceptance Criteria AC1–AC5 and Verification § Container-executable name the exact greps below.\n31\t\n32\tContainer-executability note: `python3`, `curl`, and `bash` are all installed in the image (see Dockerfile `RUN apk --no-cache add ... bash ... curl python3 ...`). The fixture server binds only `127.0.0.1` on an ephemeral port and the script under test is pointed at `SENTRY_URL=http://127.0.0.1:<port>`, so the test never touches the external network and needs no Docker or cluster tooling.\n33\t</context>\n34\t\n35\t<requirements>\n36\t1. **Create the test harness.** Create `scripts/test-sentry-read.sh`, executable (`chmod +x` to match the other `scripts/*.sh`), with `set -euo pipefail`. It must be self-contained and cwd-independent (resolve the script under test from its own directory, e.g. `SCRIPT=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)/sentry-read.sh\"`). The harness:\n37\t   - embeds the fixture server (requirement 2) via a quoted heredoc into a `$(mktemp)` file, then runs it with `python3 \"${server_py}\"` in the background;\n38\t   - captures the ephemeral port from the server's first stdout line (the server prints it once bound) by polling the server log with a bounded loop (e.g. 50 × 0.1 s sleep), failing loudly with the server log if it never appears;\n39\t   - cleans up with a `trap ... EXIT` that kills the server process and removes the temp files;\n40\t   - sets `SENTRY_API_TOKEN=x`, `SENTRY_ORG=test`, `SENTRY_URL=\"http://127.0.0.1:${PORT}\"` for every invocation of the script under test (the `x` is a dummy token — the script only requires it non-empty);\n41\t   - exits 0 only if every assertion passes, and exits non-zero with a `FAIL: <named assertion>` message (on stderr) on the first miss.\n42\t\n43\t2. **Fixture server (embedded python3).** The server routes on the request path and must serve these exact fixtures over HTTP GET on an ephemeral port bound to `127.0.0.1` (bind port 0 and print `server.server_address[1]` on stdout with `flush=True`, then `serve_forever()`):\n44\t   - Issue `123`: metadata JSON + `/events/latest/` returns an `exception` entry whose first `values[0].stacktrace.frames` is a list of exactly 40 frames. Every frame has `abs_path` (e.g. `/usr/src/app/pkg/foo/bar1.go`), `filename` (e.g. `pkg/foo/bar1.go`), a distinct numeric `lineno` (e.g. `40 + i`), a distinct `function` (e.g. `Func1`), and a `context` array whose content includes a distinctive sentinel string that never appears in the script's output, e.g. `[\"RAW-CONTEXT-SENTINEL line %d\" % i]`. This fixture drives the 30-frame cap and the no-PII checks.\n45\t   - Issue `456`: metadata JSON + `/events/latest/` returns an event with NO `exception` entry (e.g. a `message` entry only).\n46\t   - Issue `789`: metadata JSON + `/events/latest/` returns HTTP 404 (no events).\n47\t   - Issue `999`: metadata JSON + `/events/latest/` returns HTTP 401 (auth).\n48\t   - The metadata fixture has all 7 keys with distinctive values: `shortId` (e.g. `TEST-123`), `status`, `count`, `firstSeen`, `lastSeen`, `userCount`, `title`. Any other path returns 404.\n49\t   - Server must set `Content-Type: application/json` and `Content-Length`, and override `log_message` to stay quiet.\n50\t\n51\t3. **Happy-path assertions (AC1, AC2, AC3, AC5).** Run the script under test twice and capture stdout+stderr:\n52\t   - `out_bare=\"$(bash \"${SCRIPT}\" 123 2>&1)\"`\n53\t   - `out_url=\"$(bash \"${SCRIPT}\" \"http://127.0.0.1:${PORT}/api/0/organizations/test/issues/123/\" 2>&1)\"`\n54\t   Assert:\n55\t   - **AC3**: `out_bare` and `out_url` are byte-identical; neither contains `could not extract` (and the bare-id run necessarily exited 0