unt is exactly 1.\n67\t\n68\t5. **Self-check before finishing.** Re-run `<verification>` and confirm it passes. Confirm your changes are limited to `scripts/test-sentry-read.sh` (do not modify `scripts/sentry-read.sh` or any Go file). Do NOT add a CHANGELOG entry — the feature entry was added by the preceding prompt and test infrastructure is not user-facing.\n69\t</requirements>\n70\t\n71\t<constraints>\n72\t- Test-only change: do NOT modify `scripts/sentry-read.sh`, any Go code, the Config CRD, preflight, or `ALLOWED_TOOLS`.\n73\t- The test must be container-executable: python3 + curl only, fixture server on `127.0.0.1` ephemeral port, `SENTRY_URL` pointing at localhost, dummy `SENTRY_API_TOKEN=x`. No Docker socket, no external network, no real credentials.\n74\t- The assertions must encode the spec's frozen contract: 7 metadata keys in order, `file:line in function` format, 30-frame cap fixed at 30 (no cap knob), and the no-PII invariant (context lines and raw JSON never on stdout).\n75\t- The dummy token value must remain clearly non-secret (a single short placeholder like `x`) so no secret-scanner false positive.\n76\t- Do NOT commit — dark-factory handles git.\n77\t- Existing tests must still pass.\n78\t</constraints>\n79\t\n80\t<verification>\n81\tRun `bash -n scripts/test-sentry-read.sh` — must exit 0.\n82\tRun `bash scripts/test-sentry-read.sh` — must pass all assertions and exit 0.\n83\tRun `make precommit` — must exit 0 (Go suite stays green; no Go code is changed).\n84\t</verification>\n85\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8adc49446a5650c3","session_id":"5d6cc7de-1074-471b-be5a-1eef1a32f0f2","uuid":"a8505b32-40db-40ba-aa73-aa948a96784c","timestamp":"2026-08-31T22:35:04.647Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-auditor","task_description":"Audit prompt 1"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-adcc1bfc91abff4e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env bash\n2\t# Constrained read-only Sentry fetch + per-alert task publish — the watcher step\n3\t# of the Sentry pipeline.\n4\t#\n5\t# Fetches the day's active unresolved Sentry alerts and publishes one\n6\t# CreateTaskCommand per (short-id, date) via /create-tasks so the\n7\t# sentry-issue-analyzer triage agent can classify each alert.\n8\t#\n9\t# Usage: sentry-create-tasks.sh\n10\t#\n11\t# Env: SENTRY_API_TOKEN (required, Bearer token), KAFKA_BROKERS (required),\n12\t#      SENTRY_URL (default https://bborbe.sentry.io), SENTRY_ORG (default bborbe),\n13\t#      TOPIC_PREFIX (default empty), TARGET_VAULT (default personal),\n14\t#      STAGE (default dev)\n15\t#\n16\t# Read-only by construction: single GET to Sentry (issues filtered to\n17\t# is:unresolved), then a publish to Kafka. Never echoes the token.\n18\t\n19\tset -euo pipefail\n20\t\n21\t: \"${SENTRY_API_TOKEN:?SENTRY_API_TOKEN is required}\"\n22\t: \"${KAFKA_BROKERS:?KAFKA_BROKERS is required}\"\n23\tSENTRY_URL=\"${SENTRY_URL:-https://bborbe.sentry.io}\"\n24\tSENTRY_ORG=\"${SENTRY_ORG:-bborbe}\"\n25\tTOPIC_PREFIX=\"${TOPIC_PREFIX:-}\"\n26\tTARGET_VAULT=\"${TARGET_VAULT:-personal}\"\n27\tSTAGE=\"${STAGE:-dev}\"\n28\t\n29\ttmp_file=\"$(mktemp)\"\n30\tpages_file=\"$(mktemp)\"\n31\ttrap 'rm -f \"${tmp_file}\" \"${pages_file}\"' EXIT\n32\t\n33\t# Paginate the Sentry issues API (Link-header cursor) so no active unresolved\n34\t# alert is silently dropped past the first 100.\n35\tbase_url=\"${SENTRY_URL}/api/0/organizations/${SENTRY_ORG}/issues/?query=is:unresolved&limit=100\"\n36\tcursor=\"\"\n37\twhile :; do\n38\t  url=\"${base_url}\"\n39\t  if [ -n \"${cursor}\" ]; then\n40\t    url=\"${url}&cursor=${cursor}\"\n41\t  fi\n42\t  headers=\"$(mktemp)\"\n43\t  curl -fsS --max-time 30 -D \"${headers}\" \\\n44\t    -H \"Authorization: Bearer ${SENTRY_API_TOKEN}\" \\\n45\t    \"${url}\" >> \"${pages_file}\"\n46\t  printf '\\n' >> \"${pages_file}\"\n47\t  # Extract the next-page cursor + results flag from the Link header's\n48\t  # rel=\"next\" entry. Sentry always returns a next cursor, even on the last\n49\t  # page — results=\"false\" is the real \"no more pages\" signal. Breaking only\n50\t  # on an empty cursor loops forever on 0-item pages (observed 2026-08-25:\n51\t  # page 1 = 68 items, then identical 0-item pages ad infinitum).\n52\t  link=\"$(grep -i '^Link:' \"${headers}\" | head -1)\"\n53\t  cursor=\"$(printf '%s' \"${link}\" | sed -n 's/.*<[^>]*cursor=\\([^&>]*\\)[^>]*>; rel=\"next\".*/\\1/p')\"\n54\t  results=\"$(printf '%s' \"${link}\" | sed -n 's/.*; rel=\"next\"; results=\"\\([^\"]*\\)\".*/\\1/p')\"\n55\t  rm -f \"${headers}\"\n56\t  if [ -z \"${cursor}\" ] || [ \"${results}\" = \"false\" ]; then\n57\t    break\n58\t  fi\n59\tdone\n60\t\n61\t# Merge all pages into one array, then compact to the /create-tasks shape\n62\t# (project → slug string).\n63\tpython3 -c '\n64\timport json, sys\n65\tissues = []\n66\tfor line in open(sys.argv[1]):\n67\t    line = line.strip()\n68\t    if line:\n69\t        issues.extend(json.loads(line))\n70\tcompact = [{\n71\t    \"id\": issue[\"id\"],\n72\t    \"shortId\": issue[\"shortId\"],\n73\t    \"title\": issue[\"title\"],\n74\t    \"lastSeen\": issue[\"lastSeen\"],\n75\t    \"firstSeen\": issue[\"firstSeen\"],\n76\t    \"count\": issue[\"count\"],\n77\t    \"status\": issue[\"status\"],\n78\t    \"userCount\": issue[\"userCount\"],\n79\t    \"permalink\": issue[\"permalink\"],\n80\t    \"project\": issue[\"project\"][\"slug\"],\n81\t} for issue in issues]\n82\tjson.dump(compact, sys.stdout)\n83\t' \"${pages_file}\" > \"${tmp_file}\"\n84\t\n85\tcount=\"$(python3 -c 'import json, sys; print(len(json.load(open(sys.argv[1]))))' \"${tmp_file}\")\"\n86\tshort_ids=\"$(python3 -c 'import json, sys; print(\" \".join(issue[\"shortId\"] for issue in json.load(open(sys.argv[1]))))' \"${tmp_file}\")\"\n87\t\n88\techo \"sentry-create-tasks: ${count} active unresolved alerts: ${short_ids}\"\n89\t\n90\texec /create-tasks \\\n91\t  --alerts-file \"${tmp_file}\" \\\n92\t  --kafka-brokers \"${KAFKA_BROKERS}\" \\\n93\t  --topic-prefix \"${TOPIC_PREFIX}\" \\\n94\t  --target-vault \"${TARGET_VAULT}\" \\\n95\t  --stage \"${STAGE}\"\n96\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8adc49446a5650c3","session_id":"5d6cc7de-1074-471b-be5a-1eef1a32f0f2","uuid":"b2f57ba9-6f94-4c71-b7f9-f79e2fe14cb1","timestamp":"2026-08-31T22:35:04.662Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-auditor","task_description":"Audit prompt 1"}
