NTEXT-SENTINEL` exercises the no-PII invariant\n- [x] No `go mod vendor` in `<requirements>`/`<verification>` (grep-verified)\n- [x] No cross-repo writes: no `git clone`/`git push`/`gh pr` anywhere (grep-verified)\n- [x] Container-autonomous: fully executable by the container agent (bash + python3 + curl, all in the image per Dockerfile `RUN apk --no-cache add ... bash ... curl python3 ...`); no operator steps, no operator/agent split, no cluster access needed\n- [x] Sibling entry points: N/A — creates a new `scripts/test-sentry-read.sh`; no existing gate/setup function is modified. The prompt correctly guards its dependency on sibling prompt 1 (`sentry-read.sh` must already contain the `events/latest` fetch, else STOP — a correct fail-loud sequencing sentinel)\n\n## Documentation Placement\n- [x] No inlined reusable patterns (>10 lines): the fixture server and harness are described, not inlined as copyable blocks; the only inlined snippets are small assertion one-liners specific to this test\n- [x] Existing project docs referenced in `<context>`: the spec (behavioral contract AC1–AC5, Verification §) is cited; `scripts/sentry-create-tasks.sh` cited as the style reference for `mktemp`/`trap`/`python3 -c '...'`\n- [x] Coding plugin docs: N/A — no Go code in this prompt (bash-only test); no changelog doc needed since req 5 explicitly forbids a CHANGELOG entry\n- [x] Domain knowledge (output contract, fixture shapes) lives in the spec, not inlined\n\n## Code Reference Verification\n| Reference | File | Status |\n|-----------|------|--------|\n| `scripts/sentry-read.sh` (script under test; dependency guard) | `/workspace/scripts/sentry-read.sh` | Verified — exists; currently does NOT yet contain `events/latest` fetch (pre-prompt-1 state), so the context's \"STOP if out of order\" guard is correct |\n| `scripts/sentry-create-tasks.sh` (style: `mktemp`+`trap`, `python3 -c '...'`+`sys.argv[1]`) | `/workspace/scripts/sentry-create-tasks.sh` | Verified — lines 29-31, 63-83 match the described pattern exactly |\n| `specs/in-progress/001-sentry-read-event-payload.md` (AC1–AC5, Verification §, Failure Modes) | `/workspace/specs/in-progress/001-sentry-read-event-payload.md` | Verified — AC/DB/failure-table text matches every assertion in the prompt |\n| Dockerfile `apk ... bash ... curl python3` claim (context line 32) | `/workspace/Dockerfile` | Verified — `RUN apk --no-cache add ca-certificates curl bash git python3 nodejs npm` |\n\n## Coding Guidelines Compliance\n| Guideline | File | Status |\n|-----------|------|--------|\n| Go patterns / error wrapping / testing | (all `go-*.md`) | N/A — no Go code in this prompt; `make precommit` keeps the Go suite green unchanged |\n| Bash style parity with repo (`set -euo pipefail`, `mktemp` + `trap 'rm -f ...' EXIT`, `python3 -c '...' \"${file}\"`) | `/workspace/scripts/sentry-create-tasks.sh` | Compliant — req 1 and context 28 explicitly mirror the repo's established style |\n| Container-executable dependencies (busybox provides `paste`, `tr`, `grep`, `sed`, `printf`, `mktemp`; python3/curl in image) | `Dockerfile` | Compliant — all assertion-tool commands (`grep`, `paste`, `tr`, `printf`) are busybox coreutils, present in the alpine image |\n\n## YAGNI Pass (scope-creep detector)\n- [x] No opt-out flag or escape hatch negating the spec Goal — the 30-frame cap is explicitly \"fixed at 30 (no cap knob)\" (constraint line 74)\n- [x] Every fixture (123/456/789/999) maps to a spec failure mode or AC — no invented variations\n- [x] No tunable thresholds, no future-proofing knobs, no unrequested configurability. The `RAW-CONTEXT-SENTINEL` and `bar{n}.go` values are test fixtures, not knobs\n- [x] No test cases exercising a non-existent opt-out path\n\n## Critical Issues\n\n**1. Negative `grep -q` assertions written in bare form will spuriously abort the harness under its own `set -euo pipefail`.**\n- Location: requirement 3, lines 58 and 59.\n- Old text (line 58): `and the 31st+ frame files are absent (e.g. \\`grep -q 'bar31.go'\\` must fail)`\n- Old text (line 59): `no quoted JSON keys on stdout — \\`grep -qE '\"context\"|\"frames\"|stacktrace'\\` must fail — and the sentinel from the fixture's \\`context\\` arrays (e.g. \\`RAW-CONTEXT-SENTINEL\\`) must not appear in stdout.`\n\nRequirement 1 declares the harness runs `set -euo pipefail`. A bare `grep -q 'bar31.go'` that finds no match exits 1, and — being a standalone command (not inside `if`/`&&`/`!`) — triggers `set -e`, aborting the whole harness. The result: every time the assertion *passes* (31st frame absent), the test dies with a non-zero exit, so the suite can never go green. Same for `grep -qE '\"context\"|\"frames\"|stacktrace'` on line 59. A careful executor may infer the negation, but the prompt presents the bare form as the example, so it is exactly the verbatim-copy foot-gun this audit exists to catch.\n\n**Fix (find/replace):**\n- Replace line 58 with:\n  `and the 31st+ frame files are absent (e.g. \\`! grep -q 'bar31.go' <<< \"$out_bare\"\\` — note the \\`!\\` negation: a bare \\`grep -q\\` that finds nothing exits 1 and would abort the harness under its \\`set -e\\`)`\n- Replace line 59 with:\n  `no quoted JSON keys on stdout — \\`! grep -qE '\"context\"|\"frames\"|stacktrace' <<< \"$out_bare\"\\` (same \\`!\\` negation caveat as above) — and the sentinel from the fixture's \\`context\\` arrays (e.g. \\`RAW-CONTEXT-SENTINEL\\`) must not appear in stdout.`\n\n## Recommendations\n\n1. **Coverage of the `fetch failed` classification branch (Recommendation, non-blocking).** Prompt 1's decision tree has four failure reasons (`timeout`, `no events`, `auth`, `fetch failed`) plus the no-exception marker; this harness only exercises `no events` (789/404), `auth` (999/401), and no-exception (456). A cheap 500-status stub (e.g. issue `555` → `/events/latest/` returns 500) would exercise the `stack_trace unavailable (fetch failed)` branch that currently ships untested. The `timeout` branch (curl rc 28) is impractical to fixture deterministically (needs a hang longer than `--max-time 30`) and is reasonably left untested — worth a one-line comment stating that choice.\n\n2. **Metadata-before-stack-trace position is not asserted (Recommendation).** The AC1 order check (req 3) extracts the 7 metadata keys in their *relative* line order, but never asserts the metadata block precedes the `stack_trace`/frame block or the failure marker. AC4's \"never suppresses or reorders the metadata block\" would survive a reordering regression. Cheap fix: assert line 1 is `short_id=*` and that the `stack_trace` header/marker line number is > 7 (e.g. `[ \"$(printf '%s\\n' \"$out_bare\" | sed -n '1p' | grep -c '^short_id=')\" -eq 1 ]`).\n\n3. **Fixture path routing underspecified (Recommendation).** Requirement 2 says \"The server routes on the request path\" without pinning the exact path match (metadata endpoint `/api/0/organizations/test/issues/{id}/` vs `/issues/{id}/events/latest/`, and how the issue id is keyed). Since the harness also validates that `SENTRY_URL=http://127.0.0.1:${PORT}` + `SENTRY_ORG=test` produce those paths, pinning two explicit route patterns (e.g. `path.endswith('/events/latest/')` → event fixture keyed by id in path; else metadata fixture) removes the only remaining executor guess.\n\n4. **Minor: summary bullet 2 uses `file:line in function` / `stack_trace unavailable` markers.** These are the observable output contract, so acceptable, but they are format-level jargon for a \"plain-language, human reviewer\" summary. Consider \"frame lines in `file:line` format\" if a rewrite is convenient. Non-blocking.\n\n## Strengths\n- Correctly scoped as a test-only prompt: constraints forbid touching `sentry-read.sh`, Go code, CRD, preflight, and ALLOWED_TOOLS, matching the spec's Non-goals.\n- The harness design is the right shape for the boundary rule: it drives the real script through a real local HTTP server (subprocess + HTTP + exit-code boundaries), with a bounded port poll and loud named-FAIL failures — a genuine level-2 integration contract test of AC1–AC5.\n- All fixture values and assertions are mutually consistent and mentally compilable: fixture 123's 40 frames with `lineno=40+i` produce exactly `bar1.go:41 in Func1` … `bar30.go:70 in Func30`, so the `grep -c '^[^=]+:[0-9]+ in ' == 30`, `grep '^bar1.go:41 in Func1$'`, and `grep -q 'bar31.go'` (absent) assertions line up; the `stack_trace=30 frames` header does not collide with the `stacktrace` (no underscore) no-PII regex.\n- The dependency guard on sibling prompt 1 (\"if the script does NOT yet contain an events/latest fetch, STOP\") is a correct fail-loud sequencing sentinel, and the byte-identity AC3 assertion is sound because both invocations resolve to the identical URL.\n- Container-autonomy is airtight: everything runs with image-provided tools on 127.0.0.1, no git, no Docker socket, no operator handoff, no cross-repo writes.\n\n## Summary\nAn exemplary, well-scoped, container-autonomous test-locking prompt whose assertions are mutually consistent with the spec and the fixture design. One localized critical wording bug — the two negative `grep -q ... must fail` assertions, written bare under the harness's own `set -euo pipefail`, will abort the harness on the passing path — must be fixed (add `!` negation) before approval; the remaining findings are optional coverage and specificity improvements. Priority action: apply the Critical Issue find/replace on requirement 3 lines 58-59, then approve.\n\nRelevant files: `/workspace/prompts/2-spec-001-sentry-read-event-payload.md`, `/workspace/prompts/1-spec-001-sentry-read-event-payload.md`, `/workspace/specs/in-progress/001-sentry-read-event-payload.md`, `/workspace/scripts/sentry-read.sh`, `/workspace/scripts/sentry-create-tasks.sh`, `/workspace/.dark-factory.yaml`, `/workspace/.dark-factory.log`.","usage":{"total_tokens":0,"tool_uses":11,"duration_ms":106398},"uuid":"14ecb8d7-3c0a-462e-ae95-f386835ead37","session_id":"5d6cc7de-1074-471b-be5a-1eef1a32f0f2"}
