o `hideGit: true`; and the only `git` mention in the prompt is the constraint \"Do NOT commit — dark-factory handles git.\" (line 145), which is a prohibition, not a command\n- [x] No operator-only commands in `<verification>` — verified by grep: no docker/kubectl/`make buca`/`dark-factory`/`scripts/*.sh`/`gh` in verification or requirements\n- [x] File in `prompts/` inbox (not `prompts/in-progress/`)\n- [x] Filename not prefixed with dark-factory global number — `1-spec-001-sentry-read-event-payload.md` matches the allowed multi-prompt ordering pattern `^[1-9]-spec-\\d{3}-.*\\.md$` (sibling `2-` prompt confirmed present)\n- [x] Filename reflects primary change — `spec-001-sentry-read-event-payload` is the spec slug; content matches the spec's scope\n- [x] Status is `draft` (valid), frontmatter only has `spec`/`status`/`created`, `spec` uses canonical full-slug form\n\n## Failure Mode Coverage\n- [x] Spec failure modes addressed in requirements — all 8 table rows mapped:\n  - 404 → `no events` (req 3), 401/403 → `auth` (req 3), timeout → `timeout` (req 3), malformed/truncated + missing exception → `no exception entry` (req 4), metadata endpoint fails → non-zero unchanged (req 2), large payload → ≤30 frames (req 4), concurrency → per-invocation `mktemp` temp file, no shared state (req 3), clock skew → N/A\n- [x] Security concerns from spec addressed — input validation (`[0-9]+` before URL interpolation, req 1 bullet), credential handling (Bearer header only, never printed), trust-boundary (python parses read-only, three scalar fields only, req 4), PII (constraint + req 4), hangs/retries (`--max-time 30` on both GETs), rate limiting (429 → `fetch failed` marker)\n- [x] External calls have timeout/cancellation behavior specified — both GETs carry `--max-time 30`; event fetch guarded under `set +e`/`set -e` so it cannot fail the run\n- [x] New constants / strings that flow through library validators have a test calling the validator — the marker strings and frame format