isting coding plugin docs referenced — `changelog-guide.md` is referenced in `<context>` (line 31) and req 6\n- [x] Domain knowledge that outlives the prompt is in docs — the Sentry event schema detail is spec-owned; the prompt correctly defers to the spec rather than inlining knowledge other prompts will need\n\n## Code Reference Verification\n| Reference | File | Status |\n|-----------|------|--------|\n| Id-extraction sed line + comment \"Extract a numeric issue id from a URL like .../issues/1234567890/ or accept a bare id.\" | `scripts/sentry-read.sh:29-30` | Verified — matches verbatim |\n| \"single GET\" header claim to correct | `scripts/sentry-read.sh:14` | Verified — header says \"single GET\"; req 5 corrects it to two GETs |\n| Seven `printf` metadata lines + order | `scripts/sentry-read.sh:41-47` | Verified — short_id, status, live_event_count, first_seen, last_seen, users_impacted, title |\n| Usage check `usage: sentry-read.sh <issue-url-or-id>` + `exit 2` | `scripts/sentry-read.sh:24-27` | Verified |\n| `mktemp` + `trap 'rm -f ...' EXIT` and `python3 -c '...' \"${file}\"` / `sys.argv[1]` pattern | `scripts/sentry-create-tasks.sh:29-31, 63-83` | Verified |\n| Spec contract DB1–DB5, Failure Modes, Security, AC1–AC5 | `specs/in-progress/001-sentry-read-event-payload.md` | Verified — prompt's decision tree and marker strings match the spec's failure-mode table; classification is spec-derived, not author-invented |\n| Sibling mock-API test assertions | `prompts/2-spec-001-sentry-read-event-payload.md` | Verified — executed the inlined python against the sibling's 40-frame fixture; byte-for-byte output matches its regexes |\n| `changelog-guide.md` `## Unreleased` placement | `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/changelog-guide.md` | Verified — file exists; placement rule matches; repo's CHANGELOG currently has no `## Unreleased` (confirmed) |\n| `Bash(scripts/sentry-read.sh:*)` tool contract | `k8s/*.yaml`, `pkg/preflight/preflight.go` | Uncha