md` `## Unreleased` placement | `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/changelog-guide.md` | Verified — file exists; placement rule matches; repo's CHANGELOG currently has no `## Unreleased` (confirmed) |\n| `Bash(scripts/sentry-read.sh:*)` tool contract | `k8s/*.yaml`, `pkg/preflight/preflight.go` | Unchanged (path/name not modified) — no doc/config reference becomes stale |\n\n## Coding Guidelines Compliance\n| Guideline | File | Status |\n|-----------|------|--------|\n| Go guidelines (error wrapping, factories, handlers, time-injection) | `go-*.md` | N/A — no Go code in this prompt |\n| Test-only package-level mutable state | `go-composition.md` | N/A |\n| Bash style parity (set -euo pipefail, curl -fsS --max-time 30, Bearer header, mktemp+trap, python3 -c) | `scripts/sentry-read.sh` / `scripts/sentry-create-tasks.sh` | Compliant — req 1/3/4 explicitly mirror existing repo patterns |\n| `make precommit` scope | `Makefile.precommit` | Correct — single Go module at repo root; precommit (ensure/format/generate/test/check/addlicense) does not run shellcheck but keeps Go green as claimed |\n\n## YAGNI Pass (scope-creep detector)\n- [x] No opt-out flag for the very behavior the prompt ships — the constraints (line 142) explicitly reject \"a frame-count cap knob, an opt-out flag for the event fetch, or any retry/backoff logic — the cap is fixed at 30 and the fetch is always attempted\". This is the spec's Non-goal restated, and it is exactly the YAGNI guard the auditor would otherwise demand\n- [x] Every config field / threshold / branch is demanded by the spec — the only classification addition beyond the spec table is the catch-all `fetch failed` reason, which is required for completeness (Sentry 429 / 5xx on `events/latest` must map somewhere; the spec's Security section implies it). Not scope creep\n- [x] No \"future-proofing\" knobs without a named consumer\n\n## Critical Issues\nNone. All required sections present, all code references verified accurate, all spec failure modes and security items addressed across the prompt batch, no container-autonomy / hideGit / cross-repo / vendor violations, and the inlined implementation was executed and matches the sibling test's contract.\n\n## Recommendations\n1. **30-frame cap prose/code mismatch (req 4).** The inline program applies the cap to the RAW frames list first (`for frame in frames[:30]:`), then skips non-numeric `lineno`. The prose says the cap is \"the first 30 frames from `stacktrace.frames` AFTER skipping frames without a numeric `lineno`\", which implies filter-then-cap — a different iteration order. I demonstrated the divergence: with a mixed fixture (some of the first 30 frames lacking `lineno`), the code emits fewer than 30 frames even though numeric frames exist later, while the prose would emit up to 30. Both prompts' fixtures are all-numeric so tests pass either way, and the spec DB3 wording is genuinely ambiguous, but the prompt contradicts its own load-bearing code. Suggest replacing:\n   - Old: \"The 30-frame cap is the first 30 frames from `stacktrace.frames` AFTER skipping frames without a numeric `lineno`; the header `stack_trace=<N> frames` reports N = the number of emitted frame lines (N ≤ 30).\"\n   - New: \"The 30-frame cap takes the first 30 frames from `stacktrace.frames` and then skips any lacking a numeric `lineno` (matching the inline program); the header `stack_trace=<N> frames` reports N = the number of emitted frame lines (N ≤ 30).\"\n\n2. **Prompt 1 ships no behavioral test and does not reference its test sibling.** `<requirements>` changes `scripts/sentry-read.sh` and `<verification>` only checks syntax + Go-suite green; the behavioral verification (AC1–AC5) is entirely delegated to sibling prompt `2-spec-001-sentry-read-event-payload.md`. This is fine per the spec's decomposition, but prompt 1 alone reads as \"changes code with no tests\" (the DoD's test-coverage warning trigger). Suggest adding one line to req 7 or `<verification>`: \"The deterministic AC1–AC5 contract test ships in sibling prompt `2-spec-001-sentry-read-event-payload.md` (same spec batch); this prompt's verification is intentionally syntax + Go-suite only.\" Also consider flagging in the spec that the two prompts should ship as a batch before release (atomic-batch constraints belong in the spec per the global conventions).\n\n3. **Timeout / generic `fetch failed` / malformed-JSON marker branches have no contract test.** Sibling prompt 2 covers `no events`, `auth`, `no exception entry`, the 30-cap, and no-PII, but not the `timeout` (curl exit 28), generic `fetch failed`, or malformed-JSON degradation paths. These are graceful-degradation strings, so severity is low, but they are the exact class of \"marker string crossing the subprocess/stdout boundary\" the boundary-contract rule targets. Suggest adding to the sibling test a hanging stub with a short `--max-time` override (e.g. `--max-time 1`) to exercise the `timeout` branch, and a malformed-JSON fixture for `no exception entry`; if that is deemed too fiddly, note explicitly that these branches are covered only by the operator live check.\n\n4. **Spec-side doc gap (out of prompt scope, for the spec author).** The spec cites `docs/rules/scenario-writing.md` (\"When to Write a Scenario\") and asserts \"existing scenario 001\" exists — `docs/rules/` does not exist in this repo and `scenarios/001-sentry-issue-happy-path.md` is present (so the scenario claim is true, but the cited rules doc is missing). Not a prompt defect; the prompt correctly does not reference it.\n\n## Strengths\n- Load-bearing implementation is inlined verbatim (id-extraction block, curl guard, python frame extractor) and I verified each by execution: bare-id/URL/garbage argument handling and the 40-frame fixture output match the spec DB1/DB3 and sibling prompt 2's assertion regexes exactly.\n- Anchoring is exemplary: req 1 pins the exact existing sed line + comment text and shows old→new, avoiding line-number drift.\n- Cross-prompt contract consistency is real, not just claimed — the marker strings and frame format are identical between prompt 1's code and prompt 2's grep assertions.\n- Constraints are faithfully copied from the spec (agent has no memory), include \"do NOT commit\", and actively YAGNI-guard the cap-knob/opt-out/retry escapes.\n- Verification is strictly container-executable; the operator-only live checks correctly remain in the spec's operator ladder rather than leaking into the prompt.\n\n## Summary\nThis is a high-quality, well-scoped prompt with a complete DoD structure, fully verified code references, and cross-prompt test coverage in its sibling. The two marker branches (`timeout`, `fetch failed`) lack a contract test and req 4's cap-ordering prose contradicts its own inline code, but neither threatens the shipped behavior. Recommended action: apply Recommendation 1's find/replace (prose alignment) and add the sibling cross-reference from Recommendation 2 before approving; no critical blockers.\n\nRelevant files (absolute paths): `/workspace/prompts/1-spec-001-sentry-read-event-payload.md`, `/workspace/prompts/2-spec-001-sentry-read-event-payload.md`, `/workspace/specs/in-progress/001-sentry-read-event-payload.md`, `/workspace/scripts/sentry-read.sh`, `/workspace/scripts/sentry-create-tasks.sh`, `/workspace/.dark-factory.yaml`, `/workspace/Makefile.precommit`, `/workspace/CHANGELOG.md`.\n\n### prompts/2-spec-001-sentry-read-event-payload.md\n\n# Prompt Audit Report: Add a deterministic mock-API test for the Sentry read script\n\n**File**: `/workspace/prompts/2-spec-001-sentry-read-event-payload.md`\n**Score**: 8/10\n**Status**: Good — one localized critical wording bug, otherwise exemplary\n\n## DoD Checklist\n- [x] `<summary>` present and plain-language (6 bullets, observable outcomes; minor format-string jargon — see Recommendations)\n- [x] `<objective>` states end state, not steps (1 sentence, what + why)\n- [x] `<context>` present; references only existing files; correctly states \"no project-level CLAUDE.md\" (verified — no `/workspace/CLAUDE.md`)\n- [x] `<requirements>` numbered and specific (5 steps, exact file paths, command forms)\n- [x] `<constraints>` present, copied from spec (frozen 7-key order, 30-frame cap with \"no cap knob\", no-PII, dummy token `x`, \"Do NOT commit\", existing tests stay green)\n- [x] `<verification>` present with runnable container-executable commands (`bash -n`, `bash scripts/test-sentry-read.sh`, `make precommit`)\n- [x] All paths repo-relative (`scripts/sentry-read.sh`, `scripts/sentry-create-tasks.sh`, `specs/in-progress/001-sentry-read-event-payload.md` — all verified to exist). No `/Users/`, `/home/`, `~/`, or `$HOME` paths anywhere (grep-verified).\n- [x] No bare `git ` commands in `<verification>` or `<requirements>` (grep-verified). Note: `.dark-factory.log` shows `hideGit=true` is active (source=arg), so git is masked in the container — but the prompt contains zero git commands, so no violation.\n- [x] No operator-only commands in `<verification>` (`docker`, `make buca`, `dark-factory`, `kubectl*`, `scripts/*.sh`, `gh ...` — grep-verified clean)\n- [x] File in `prompts/` inbox, not `prompts/in-progress/` (verified — `prompts/in-progress/` is empty)\n- [x] Filename not prefixed with dark-factory global number; `2-spec-001-...` matches the allowed multi-prompt ordering pattern `^[1-9]-spec-\\d{3}-.*\\.md$` (sibling `1-spec-001-...` exists)\n- [x] Filename reflects primary change (deterministic mock-API test; matches `<objective>`/`<summary>`)\n- [x] `status: draft` (valid inbox status)\n- [x] Frontmatter: `spec: [\"001-sentry-read-event-payload\"]` canonical full-slug form, only `spec`/`status`/`created` fields — compliant\n\n## Failure Mode Coverage\n- [x] Spec failure triggers addressed across the prompt set (spec's Suggested Decomposition: prompt 1 implements, prompt 2 tests):\n  - 404 no events → req 4 `out_404` → `stack_trace unavailable (no events)` ✓\n  - 401/403 auth → req 4 `out_auth` → `stack_trace unavailable (auth)` ✓\n  - no exception entry → req 4 `out_noexc` → `stack_trace unavailable (no exception entry)` ✓ (fixture 456 drives the extraction-empty path)\n  - timeout → implemented in sibling prompt 1 (curl rc 28 → `timeout`); not fixture-tested (see Recommendations)\n  - metadata-fetch failure → explicitly preserved in sibling prompt 1 req 2 (\"do not touch\"); unchanged existing behavior, not re-tested (acceptable per scope note)\n- [x] Security concerns from spec addressed: no-PII invariant asserted (AC5 greps), dummy non-secret token `x` required by constraint, no input-interpolation surface changed (test-only)\n- [x] External calls have timeout/cancellation: fixture binds 127.0.0.1 ephemeral port, harness port-poll is bounded (50 × 0.1 s), script-under-test carries `--max-time 30`; no unbounded loops\n- [x] Boundary-contract tests: this prompt IS the boundary test — it drives the real script through a real local HTTP server (subprocess + HTTP + exit-code boundaries). Level-2 integration testing of the exact output contract; fixture 123's 40 frames exercise the 30-cap, `RAW-CONTEXT-SENTINEL` exercises the no-PII invariant\n- [x] No `go mod vendor` in `<requirements>`/`<verification>` (grep-verified)\n- [x] No cross-repo writes: no `git clone`/`git push`/`gh pr` anywhere (grep-verified)\n- [x] Container-autonomous: fully executable by the container agent (bash + python3 + curl, all in the image per Dockerfile `RUN apk --no-cache add ... bash ... curl python3 ...`); no operator steps, no operator/agent split, no cluster access needed\n- [x] Sibling entry points: N/A — creates a new `scripts/test-sentry-read.sh`; no existing gate/setup function is modified. The prompt correctly guards its dependency on sibling prompt 1 (`sentry-read.sh` must already contain the `events/latest` fetch, else STOP — a correct fail-loud sequencing sentinel)\n\n## Documentation Placement\n- [x] No inlined reusable patterns (>10 lines): the fixture server and harness are described, not inlined as copyable blocks; the only inlined snippets are small assertion one-liners specific to this test\n- [x] Existing project docs referenced in `<context>`: the spec (behavioral contract AC1–AC5, Verification §) is cited; `scripts/sentry-create-tasks.sh` cited as the style reference for `mktemp`/`trap`/`python3 -c '...'`\n- [x] Coding plugin docs: N/A — no Go code in this prompt (bash-only test); no changelog doc needed since req 5 explicitly forbids a CHANGELOG entry\n- [x] Domain knowledge (output contract, fixture shapes) lives in the spec, not inlined\n\n## Code Reference Verification\n| Reference | File | Status |\n|-----------|------|--------|\n| `scripts/sentry-read.sh` (script under test; dependency guard) | `/workspace/scripts/sentry-read.sh` | Verified — exists; currently does NOT yet contain `events/latest` fetch (pre-prompt-1 state), so the context's \"STOP if out of order\" guard is correct |\n| `scripts/sentry-create-tasks.sh` (style: `mktemp`+`trap`, `python3 -c '...'`+`sys.argv[1]`) | `/workspace/scripts/sentry-create-tasks.sh` | Verified — lines 29-31, 63-83 match the described pattern exactly |\n| `specs/in-progress/001-sentry-read-event-payload.md` (AC1–AC5, Verification §, Failure Modes) | `/workspace/specs/in-progress/001-sentry-read-event-payload.md` | Verified — AC/DB/failure-table text matches every assertion in the prompt |\n| Dockerfile `apk ... bash ... curl python3` claim (context line 32) | `/workspace/Dockerfile` | Verified — `RUN apk --no-cache add ca-certificates curl bash git python3 nodejs npm` |\n\n## Coding Guidelines Compliance\n| Guideline | File | Status |\n|-----------|------|--------|\n| Go patterns / error wrapping / testing | (all `go-*.md`) | N/A — no Go code in this prompt; `make precommit` keeps the Go suite green unchanged |\n| Bash style parity with repo (`set -euo pipefail`, `mktemp` + `trap 'rm -f ...' EXIT`, `python3 -c '...' \"${file}\"`) | `/workspace/scripts/sentry-create-tasks.sh` | Compliant — req 1 and context 28 explicitly mirror the repo's established style |\n| Container-executable dependencies (busybox provides `paste`, `tr`, `grep`, `sed`, `printf`, `mktemp`; python3/curl in image) | `Dockerfile` | Compliant — all assertion-tool commands (`grep`, `paste`, `tr`, `printf`) are busybox coreutils, present in the alpine image |\n\n## YAGNI Pass (scope-creep detector)\n- [x] No opt-out flag or escape hatch negating the spec Goal — the 30-frame cap is explicitly \"fixed at 30 (no cap knob)\" (constraint line 74)\n- [x] Every fixture (123/456/789/999) maps to a spec failure mode or AC — no invented variations\n- [x] No tunable thresholds, no future-proofing knobs, no unrequested configurability. The `RAW-CONTEXT-SENTINEL` and `bar{n}.go` values are test fixtures, not knobs\n- [x] No test cases exercising a non-existent opt-out path\n\n## Critical Issues\n\n**1. Negative `grep -q` assertions written in bare form will spuriously abort the harness under its own `set -euo pipefail`.**\n- Location: requirement 3, lines 58 and 59.\n- Old text (line 58): `and the 31st+ frame files are absent (e.g. \\`grep -q 'bar31.go'\\` must fail)`\n- Old text (line 59): `no quoted JSON keys on stdout — \\`grep -qE '\"context\"|\"frames\"|stacktrace'\\` must fail — and the sentinel from the fixture's \\`context\\` arrays (e.g. \\`RAW-CONTEXT-SENTINEL\\`) must not appear in stdout.`\n\nRequirement 1 declares the harness runs `set -euo pipefail`. A bare `grep -q 'bar31.go'` that finds no match exits 1, and — being a standalone command (not inside `if`/`&&`/`!`) — triggers `set -e`, aborting the whole harness. The result: every time the assertion *passes* (31st frame absent), the test dies with a non-zero exit, so the suite can never go green. Same for `grep -qE '\"context\"|\"frames\"|stacktrace'` on line 59. A careful executor may infer the negation, but the prompt presents the bare form as the example, so it is exactly the verbatim-copy foot-gun this audit exists to catch.\n\n**Fix (find/replace):**\n- Replace line 58 with:\n  `and the 31st+ frame files are absent (e.g. \\`! grep -q 'bar31.go' <<< \"$out_bare\"\\` — note the \\`!\\` negation: a bare \\`grep -q\\` that finds nothing exits 1 and would abort the harness under its \\`set -e\\`)`\n- Replace line 59 with:\n  `no quoted JSON keys on stdout — \\`! grep -qE '\"context\"|\"frames\"|stacktrace' <<< \"$out_bare\"\\` (same \\`!\\` negation caveat as above) — and the sentinel from the fixture's \\`context\\` arrays (e.g. \\`RAW-CONTEXT-SENTINEL\\`) must not appear in stdout.`\n\n## Recommendations\n\n1. **Coverage of the `fetch failed` classification branch (Recommendation, non-blocking).** Prompt 1's decision tree has four failure reasons (`timeout`, `no events`, `auth`, `fetch failed`) plus the no-exception marker; this harness only exercises `no events` (789/404), `auth` (999/401), and no-exception (456). A cheap 500-status stub (e.g. issue `555` → `/events/latest/` returns 500) would exercise the `stack_trace unavailable (fetch failed)` branch that currently ships untested. The `timeout` branch (curl rc 28) is impractical to fixture deterministically (needs a hang longer than `--max-time 30`) and is reasonably left untested — worth a one-line comment stating that choice.\n\n2. **Metadata-before-stack-trace position is not asserted (Recommendation).** The AC1 order check (req 3) extracts the 7 metadata keys in their *relative* line order, but never asserts the metadata block precedes the `stack_trace`/frame block or the failure marker. AC4's \"never suppresses or reorders the metadata block\" would survive a reordering regression. Cheap fix: assert line 1 is `short_id=*` and that the `stack_trace` header/marker line number is > 7 (e.g. `[ \"$(printf '%s\\n' \"$out_bare\" | sed -n '1p' | grep -c '^short_id=')\" -eq 1 ]`).\n\n3. **Fixture path routing underspecified (Recommendation).** Requirement 2 says \"The server routes on the request path\" without pinning the exact path match (metadata endpoint `/api/0/organizations/test/issues/{id}/` vs `/issues/{id}/events/latest/`, and how the issue id is keyed). Since the harness also validates that `SENTRY_URL=http://127.0.0.1:${PORT}` + `SENTRY_ORG=test` produce those paths, pinning two explicit route patterns (e.g. `path.endswith('/events/latest/')` → event fixture keyed by id in path; else metadata fixture) removes the only remaining executor guess.\n\n4. **Minor: summary bullet 2 uses `file:line in function` / `stack_trace unavailable` markers.** These are the observable output contract, so acceptable, but they are format-level jargon for a \"plain-language, human reviewer\" summary. Consider \"frame lines in `file:line` format\" if a rewrite is convenient. Non-blocking.\n\n## Strengths\n- Correctly scoped as a test-only prompt: constraints forbid touching `sentry-read.sh`, Go code, CRD, preflight, and ALLOWED_TOOLS, matching the spec's Non-goals.\n- The harness design is the right shape for the boundary rule: it drives the real script through a real local HTTP server (subprocess + HTTP + exit-code boundaries), with a bounded port poll and loud named-FAIL failures — a genuine level-2 integration contract test of AC1–AC5.\n- All fixture values and assertions are mutually consistent and mentally compilable: fixture 123's 40 frames with `lineno=40+i` produce exactly `bar1.go:41 in Func1` … `bar30.go:70 in Func30`, so the `grep -c '^[^=]+:[0-9]+ in ' == 30`, `grep '^bar1.go:41 in Func1$'`, and `grep -q 'bar31.go'` (absent) assertions line up; the `stack_trace=30 frames` header does not collide with the `stacktrace` (no underscore) no-PII regex.\n- The dependency guard on sibling prompt 1 (\"if the script does NOT yet contain an events/latest fetch, STOP\") is a correct fail-loud sequencing sentinel, and the byte-identity AC3 assertion is sound because both invocations resolve to the identical URL.\n- Container-autonomy is airtight: everything runs with image-provided tools on 127.0.0.1, no git, no Docker socket, no operator handoff, no cross-repo writes.\n\n## Summary\nAn exemplary, well-scoped, container-autonomous test-locking prompt whose assertions are mutually consistent with the spec and the fixture design. One localized critical wording bug — the two negative `grep -q ... must fail` assertions, written bare under the harness's own `set -euo pipefail`, will abort the harness on the passing path — must be fixed (add `!` negation) before approval; the remaining findings are optional coverage and specificity improvements. Priority action: apply the Critical Issue find/replace on requirement 3 lines 58-59, then approve.\n\nRelevant files: `/workspace/prompts/2-spec-001-sentry-read-event-payload.md`, `/workspace/prompts/1-spec-001-sentry-read-event-payload.md`, `/workspace/specs/in-progress/001-sentry-read-event-payload.md`, `/workspace/scripts/sentry-read.sh`, `/workspace/scripts/sentry-create-tasks.sh`, `/workspace/.dark-factory.yaml`, `/workspace/.dark-factory.log`.\n\n---\n\n**Note:** Per the command instructions, I did not retry, rewrite, or merge prompts based on audit findings — the human reviewer owns that decision. Both prompt files remain in `prompts/` unchanged, and the spec stays at its current status (`approved`; the `mark-prompted` transition was intentionally skipped because `DARK_FACTORY_MANAGED=true`).","ttft_ms":2221,"ttft_stream_ms":707,"time_to_request_ms":74,"type":"result","duration_ms":371201,"uuid":"88b61acf-643d-40b9-a52d-acd3cdfd68f9"}
